    // Now try to actually perform request using std TcpStream to get response
    // If connect fails, return error similar to original: "Error: Connection refused (os error 111)" etc.
    // For http2 version, original returns "Error: http2 error" if server not supporting h2.
    if use_http2 && !url_str.starts_with("https") {
        // Try to detect h2: if http version 2, we attempt to do HTTP/2? But our simple server is http1, so we should simulate http2 error.
